#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166603 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6e692dca-1bbc-59e7-999f-4acb806ddd38" :question/math-academy-id "e-8369" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =7\\arcsch(1-x),$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcsch x) = -\\dfrac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡(1-x)) \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|1-x|\\sqrt{1+(1-x)^{2}}})\\cdot (1-x)^{′} \\\\  & =7(-\\frac{1}{|x-1|\\sqrt{1+1-2x+{x}^{2}}})\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{|x-1|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-2x+2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd5d1a-eeae-58f5-b7a1-a6a20fb02df9" :question/math-academy-id "e-8370" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y =  5\\arsech{2x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arsech x) = -\\dfrac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-x^2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡2x) \\\\  & =5(-\\frac{1}{(2x)\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}})\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166605 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/id #uuid "83b6c061-a8fc-5628-a199-60196b904407" :question/math-academy-id "e-8371" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $y = \\arcoth{e^x},$ then $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\arcoth x) = \\dfrac{1}{1-x^2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({e}^{x})^{2}}\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{e}^{2x}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{x}}{1-{e}^{2x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166606 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/id #uuid "8a1806e8-d99d-5107-aa63-0bf841cb44c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8372" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIf $f(x) = \\sin{x} \\cdot \\arcsch{x},$ then $f'(x) = \\cos{x} \\arcsch{x} + g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$  is a product $u(x) \\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x) = \\sin{x}$ and $v(x) = \\arcsch{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x+{{(-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}})}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x) = -\\dfrac{\\sin{x}}{|x|\\sqrt{1+x^2}}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c37ca8aa-0613-5e1f-9137-f76eabfd3b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525702}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c37ca8aa-0613-5e1f-9137-f76eabfd3b55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525702} :answer-field/id #uuid "640512e5-7436-50c7-aa28-fc64598aa17a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525893}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ada52c09-5dae-5593-aecd-e855669a9070" :question/math-academy-id "q-313244" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2)-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(3x-2),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{3x-2}(1\\,+$\n{{field-1}}$)$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2)-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(3x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x-2))\\,-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(3x-2)) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}-(-\\frac{1}{(3x-2)\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}}})\\cdot (3x-2)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}\\,+\\,\\frac{1}{(3x-2)\\sqrt{1-(3x-2)^{2}}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x-2}(1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\,1-(3x-2)^{2}\\,}}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a37e726d-bc2a-5673-bfc6-c4c9c7ba2754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+(\\ln(x))^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a37e726d-bc2a-5673-bfc6-c4c9c7ba2754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+(\\ln(x))^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525622} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc44b4dd-a212-5cf1-811f-8d6f7f853e3f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525943}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4b717300-ca17-51b3-997a-8770eb9ed2a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-341490" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)],$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $x>0.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{x|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|}$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\{arcsch[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]\\} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|\\sqrt{1+[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]^{2}}}\\cdot [\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|\\sqrt{1+[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{x|\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)|}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)]^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525999 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5cb85dd-567f-5bb4-ab11-de246de83337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1-x^4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5cb85dd-567f-5bb4-ab11-de246de83337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1-x^4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525674} :answer-field/id #uuid "904afa00-d66a-572e-addf-a5de2b1dbe0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2dec0d91-0541-5bbd-ae10-733112238fa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-341502" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2}),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[2\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2})] \\\\  & =2\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{({x}^{2})}^{2}}}]\\cdot {({x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{4}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166766 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "216296fc-1ce3-532f-b96c-3d352c6b6ef2" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Sech Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e67cc83-f465-5d42-b43b-6441e417691b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e67cc83-f465-5d42-b43b-6441e417691b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525236} :answer-field/id #uuid "6414cbd2-14eb-5b21-9943-2ffe1ac91744" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e86ab85e-46b5-5037-89df-518112577fe7" :question/math-academy-id "q-341504" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-1)+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}[1-$\n{{field-1}} $]$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-1)+\\operatorname{arsech}⁡({x}^{2}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{{({x}^{2}-1)}^{′}}{{x}^{2}-1}-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}-1)\\sqrt{1-{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}}}\\cdot {({x}^{2}-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}-1)\\sqrt{1-({x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}+1)}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}-1)\\sqrt{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}-1}[1-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})}}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526004 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6663c7f-cb91-5adb-8520-573e1495df25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(2-3x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525676}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6663c7f-cb91-5adb-8520-573e1495df25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x(2-3x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525676} :answer-field/id #uuid "515633b7-5d08-5c5d-9a69-cebb8b7b7dcd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525887}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33a6f526-b75f-5ead-a328-98ce3a61e817" :question/math-academy-id "q-341523" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(3x-1)^{2}}\\cdot (3x-1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-(1-6x+9{x}^{2})}\\cdot (3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{6x-9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3x(2-3x)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x(2-3x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526073 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5240b319-0dfa-542f-9fdc-3bc4f72e7bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x(x^2-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525420}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5240b319-0dfa-542f-9fdc-3bc4f72e7bc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x(x^2-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525420} :answer-field/id #uuid "84cfeb38-d49f-5119-8239-d82b41a65ba4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525911}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b997ab13-f489-5c01-b9dd-74963fbbdc33" :question/math-academy-id "q-341533" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}-1),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}-1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{2}-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {({x}^{2}-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({x}^{4}-2{x}^{2}+1)}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{2{x}^{2}-{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}(2-{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x(2-{x}^{2})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186525990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2714853-7020-594c-83a2-daf04d42e112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2714853-7020-594c-83a2-daf04d42e112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{\\sqrt{1-4x^2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525812} :answer-field/id #uuid "69ac6f6a-864a-510b-ab52-fe182c5c37c0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525895}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "198c9de8-ff94-5b1b-9df3-bdbe404e2b21" :question/math-academy-id "q-341557" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{3}\\,\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x),$ calculate ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)\\,-$ \n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a product $u(x)\\cdot v(x)$ with $u(x)={x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x).$\n\nTherefore, we apply the product rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & ={({x}^{3})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)+{x}^{3}\\cdot {[\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)]}^{′} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)\\,+\\,{x}^{3}\\cdot [-\\frac{(2x)^{′}}{2x\\sqrt{1-(2x)^{2}}}] \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)+{x}^{3}\\cdot (-\\frac{2}{2x\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{arsech}⁡(2x)-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167347 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77f2bd57-160d-59ec-a8d7-087063a979f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x({x}^{2}+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525507} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb895d2-a4af-5214-ab45-6f92e193f553" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x+1}{1-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525514} {:answer/id #uuid "91c497d1-167d-5767-86ba-2e0892d1bad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x(x+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525574} {:answer/id #uuid "b24ffa9f-adae-566c-b8b0-1ff8c017e5ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525659} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a6722d-e271-5af1-a555-f03ea5081bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77f2bd57-160d-59ec-a8d7-087063a979f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{x({x}^{2}+2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525507} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb858b8a-7da0-525a-b444-dc31897715bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165291}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7ac3e918-2f81-569e-8090-bd265690a59a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95341" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}+1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡({x}^{2}+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot ({x}^{2}+1)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{1-({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{1-({x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{x({x}^{2}+2)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5e40340-35cf-50ee-8a0d-7eb873490693" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Inverse Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product and Quotient Rules"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d53b945-1cc7-5c2b-9b66-361b23b2dcec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525271} {:answer/id #uuid "46929c9e-10fd-5db5-b3e7-f2e7e9fb1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525383} {:answer/id #uuid "507c0a28-9bb1-5b5c-80ad-8483a5f402f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525414} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe0e930-bdc1-59e8-9bad-2838d6cc6692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3x(1-{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525569} {:answer/id #uuid "b947c4c6-3d0e-58cc-b4f2-207b1c280239" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x(1+{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46929c9e-10fd-5db5-b3e7-f2e7e9fb1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525383} :answer-field/id #uuid "c55b12a9-d490-5b9e-a4aa-41e0c6ac6898" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165303}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c64b6497-cde2-5c37-b145-e4237792aec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95345" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{x}^{2}},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=g(x)-\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x$ and $v(x)={x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{′}}{({x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot {x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot ({x}^{2})^{′}}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}}{{x}^{2}}-\\frac{\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x\\cdot (2x)}{{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot (\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)^{′}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{x}^{3}} \\\\  & ={{\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}-\\frac{2\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x}{{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}(1-{x}^{2})}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526027 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166765 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "319572db-8eed-59f2-95c4-d21a63642eb8" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Csch Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d0502bf-4b7b-56bd-8f60-e6aa2b4b7732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{e}^{x}\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525516} {:answer/id #uuid "9c744cb0-6b47-5126-beaa-1ffdb2fe62d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525603} {:answer/id #uuid "b27f2561-56c9-5fb2-a134-f7c789829f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525663} {:answer/id #uuid "c21ad8f6-9fc1-5677-b4dd-5a3533961f50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525699} {:answer/id #uuid "d04f1fd6-e00c-5a6b-88a6-8306fd6e0fb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{x}}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525723}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c744cb0-6b47-5126-beaa-1ffdb2fe62d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525603} :answer-field/id #uuid "26881df5-9845-5126-b23c-a867fbea3cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525865}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61b524cd-3bec-51a5-bff2-353476be186c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95514" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=-4\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{|{e}^{x}|\\sqrt{1+{({e}^{x})}^{2}}})\\cdot ({e}^{x})^{′} \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{{e}^{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}\\cdot {e}^{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{1+{e}^{2x}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186526070 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74aa4936-437c-52c6-b5ec-f175443379a7" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating an Inverse Coth Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0716eb87-422e-5cce-99ca-7fa7c2aa38ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}(\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{6}}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525222} {:answer/id #uuid "234d1a8b-ede3-548a-84a3-6a80aa419f10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525288} {:answer/id #uuid "244fda9d-e992-5a40-bfe5-837ada8a932b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-{x}^{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525293} {:answer/id #uuid "2a122d3d-ad7b-5b97-9691-3b6ba2f22261" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525307} {:answer/id #uuid "8528dc6b-7321-5ec2-a530-b799e7656289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8528dc6b-7321-5ec2-a530-b799e7656289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525541} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64afe9f-ff1b-5a4d-ada7-a63884592d75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186525961}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ae0e06e0-ba79-5c50-9e53-bfbd25cee78e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95542" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{x}^{3}-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡{x}^{3})-\\frac{3}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{({x}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot ({x}^{3})^{′}-\\frac{3}{4}(4{x}^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3} \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{6}}-x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
